I found and fixed the bug in src/parse.py:4. The issue was an off-by-one error where the function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`. Since Python uses 0-based indexing, the first element of a list is at index 0, not index 1. This was causing the function to return the second word instead of the first word, and also causing an IndexError when there was only a single word.
